#. type: Title #
#: docs/api-guide.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Connecting an inventory tool"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/api-guide.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "A walkthrough for the developers of a program that prints labels through the print server, here an inventory tool that prints asset labels: one label, a series of labels in one request, following the job, printing again after a jam, and handling errors. Every request is described in the [API reference](api.md); setting up the server in [Server installation](server-install.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/api-guide.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The setup { #setup }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/api-guide.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "The examples use these names; yours will differ:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/api-guide.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "The server: `https://labels.example.com/api/v1`, reached through the company's reverse proxy."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/api-guide.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "The label `asset-tag.tavletta` in the labels folder, designed in the Tavletta app, with a QR code and a text that both contain the placeholder `{AssetNumber}`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/api-guide.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "The printer `it-cab` of `printers.toml`: a cab label printer with thermal transfer (`method = \"transfer\"`), printing turned by 180 degrees (`upside_down = true`)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/api-guide.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "An access token with the role `print`, limited to `it-cab`, made by the server's administrator:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: docs/api-guide.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  tavletta token new inventory-tool --role print --printer it-cab \\\n"
"      --tokens tokens.toml --printers printers.toml\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/api-guide.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Keep the token in the tool's secret store (configuration encrypted, a vault), not in the code. In the shell examples:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: docs/api-guide.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"TAVLETTA=https://labels.example.com/api/v1\n"
"TOKEN=tav_3f9c0a1b2c4d_Xq2…\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/api-guide.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "1. What the label needs { #describe }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: docs/api-guide.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "curl -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" \"$TAVLETTA/labels/asset-tag\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/api-guide.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "The answer lists the label's `columns` (here `[\"AssetNumber\"]`): every data row needs these keys. A placeholder without a value in the row refuses the print with 422 `label_unprintable` (\"No such column\"), so a label never prints a half-empty text."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/api-guide.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "2. Preview { #preview }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/api-guide.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "A preview prints nothing and returns the label as a PNG image, for example to show it in the tool before printing:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: docs/api-guide.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"curl -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n"
"     -d '{\"label\": \"asset-tag\", \"printer\": \"it-cab\", \"data_rows\": [{\"AssetNumber\": \"100001\"}]}' \\\n"
"     -o preview.png \"$TAVLETTA/preview\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/api-guide.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "With `\"format\": \"json\"` the answer is JSON with the image in base64 and the `warnings` (for example `font_missing`, `barcode_narrow`)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/api-guide.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "`\"view\": \"printer\"` shows the image as the printer gets it (turned)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/api-guide.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "A preview needs only the role `preview`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/api-guide.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "3. Print one label { #one }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: docs/api-guide.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"curl -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n"
"     -d '{\"label\": \"asset-tag\", \"printer\": \"it-cab\", \"data_rows\": [{\"AssetNumber\": \"100001\"}], \"wait\": 30}' \\\n"
"     \"$TAVLETTA/print\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/api-guide.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "The server checks the request, queues a job for the printer and answers with the job. With `\"wait\": 30` it waits up to 30 seconds for the job: 200 with `\"state\": \"done\"` once printed, else 202 with the job still `queued` or `printing`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/api-guide.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "The answer's `Location` header and the job's `id` lead to `GET /api/v1/jobs/{id}`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/api-guide.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Each printer prints one job after the other; jobs of different printers run side by side."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/api-guide.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "4. A series in one request { #series }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/api-guide.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Twenty asset labels are one request with twenty data rows, not twenty requests: they print as one job, in order, and a problem stops the job at a known row."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: docs/api-guide.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"curl -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n"
"     -d '{\"label\": \"asset-tag\", \"printer\": \"it-cab\", \"wait\": 60,\n"
"          \"data_rows\": [{\"AssetNumber\": \"100001\"}, {\"AssetNumber\": \"100002\"},\n"
"                        {\"AssetNumber\": \"100003\"}, {\"AssetNumber\": \"100020\"}]}' \\\n"
"     \"$TAVLETTA/print\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/api-guide.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "The recommended pattern: **the tool owns the numbers.** The tool takes the next free asset numbers from its own database, saves them with the assets, and sends them as data rows. The label never counts by itself, so a second server, a restored backup or a reprint can never hand out a number twice."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/api-guide.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The alternative: the label's counter { #counter }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/api-guide.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "A label with the variable `{=counter}` (for example `{=counter:000000}` for six digits) counts by itself. The tool can still say where to start:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: docs/api-guide.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"curl -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n"
"     -d '{\"label\": \"asset-tag-counter\", \"printer\": \"it-cab\",\n"
"          \"counter_start\": 100001, \"copies\": 20, \"no_save_counter\": true}' \\\n"
"     \"$TAVLETTA/print\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/api-guide.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "`counter_start` is the first number; the counter goes up with every label and copy: 100001 to 100020."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/api-guide.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "`no_save_counter`: the server does not save the next number into the label file. Without it, the label file keeps the next number (100021), and the next print without `counter_start` goes on from there."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/api-guide.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Use this only when the numbers do not need to be in the tool's database before printing."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/api-guide.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "5. Follow the job { #job }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: docs/api-guide.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "curl -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" \"$TAVLETTA/jobs/$JOB\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/api-guide.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| `state` | Meaning |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| `queued` | waits for the printer |\n"
"| `waiting` | waits for the label file (another job is saving its counter) |\n"
"| `printing` | is printing; `printed` of `total` labels are out |\n"
"| `done` | all labels printed |\n"
"| `failed` | stopped: `error` says why, `rows_printed` how far it came |\n"
"| `canceled` | canceled |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/api-guide.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Ask every one or two seconds while the state is not final; the server keeps finished jobs for 24 hours."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/api-guide.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "A `print` token sees its own jobs only; another token's job is \"not found\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/api-guide.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "6. After a jam: print the rest { #reprint }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/api-guide.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "When the printer runs out of labels or jams, the job fails, for example:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (json)
#: docs/api-guide.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{\"state\": \"failed\", \"printed\": 13, \"total\": 20, \"rows_printed\": 13,\n"
" \"error\": {\"code\": \"printer_out_of_labels\",\n"
"           \"message\": \"… Printing stopped at row 14. To continue, print again from row 14.\"}}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/api-guide.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Once the printer is ready, send the same request again with `rows`, the rows still missing:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: docs/api-guide.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"curl -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n"
"     -d '{\"label\": \"asset-tag\", \"printer\": \"it-cab\", \"rows\": \"14-20\",\n"
"          \"data_rows\": [{\"AssetNumber\": \"100001\"}, {\"AssetNumber\": \"100020\"}]}' \\\n"
"     \"$TAVLETTA/print\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/api-guide.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "`rows` counts the data rows from 1: `\"14-20\"`, `\"14-\"` (to the last), `\"5\"`. Send the same data rows as before, so row 14 is the same asset.  A label that was half printed when the printer stopped belongs to the row that failed and is printed again."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/api-guide.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "7. Cancel { #cancel }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: docs/api-guide.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "curl -X DELETE -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" \"$TAVLETTA/jobs/$JOB\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/api-guide.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "A queued job is canceled at once; a printing one stops after the label being printed. 409 `job_finished` if it had finished already."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/api-guide.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "8. Retries and errors { #errors }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/api-guide.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "`POST /print` is not idempotent: a request sent twice prints twice. So:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/api-guide.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Retry automatically** only answers that were refused before a job was made: 503 `busy` and 429 `queue_full`, after a pause that grows (1, 2, 4, 8 s)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/api-guide.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Do not retry automatically** when the connection broke or timed out after the request was sent: the job may exist and print. Show the operator what happened, let them check the printer, then print the missing labels with `rows`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/api-guide.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Fix the request** for other 4xx answers; the code says what is wrong:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/api-guide.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Code | What the tool does |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| `unauthorized` (401) | Token wrong, expired or revoked: ask the administrator for a new one. |\n"
"| `forbidden` (403) | The token's role is too low. |\n"
"| `printer_not_found`, `label_not_found` (404) | Name typed wrong, or the token may not use that printer. |\n"
"| `invalid_field`, `unknown_field` (400) | A bug in the tool: the message names the field. |\n"
"| `too_many_copies` (400), `too_many_labels` (413) | Split the series into several jobs. |\n"
"| `label_unprintable` (422) | The data does not fit the label (a missing column, a code that cannot hold the value): show the message. |\n"
"| `busy` (503), `queue_full` (429) | Retry after a pause. |\n"
"| `printer_<code>` in a failed job | Show the message to the operator; continue with `rows` once fixed. |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/api-guide.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "The message (`error.message`) is in the language of `Accept-Language` and meant for people: show it, but decide by the code."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/api-guide.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Example: Python { #python }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/api-guide.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "With the `requests` package:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (python)
#: docs/api-guide.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"import os\n"
"import time\n"
"\n"
"import requests\n"
"\n"
"BASE = os.environ.get(\"TAVLETTA\", \"https://labels.example.com/api/v1\")\n"
"TOKEN = os.environ[\"TAVLETTA_TOKEN\"]  # from the secret store, never in the code\n"
"FINAL = {\"done\", \"failed\", \"canceled\"}\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"class LabelError(Exception):\n"
"    def __init__(self, status, code, message):\n"
"        super().__init__(\"%s %s: %s\" % (status, code, message))\n"
"        self.status, self.code = status, code\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"session = requests.Session()\n"
"session.headers.update({\"Authorization\": \"Bearer \" + TOKEN, \"Accept-Language\": \"de-CH\"})\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"def call(method, path, **kwargs):\n"
"    response = session.request(method, BASE + path, timeout=330, **kwargs)\n"
"    if response.status_code >= 400:\n"
"        try:\n"
"            error = response.json()[\"error\"]\n"
"        except (ValueError, KeyError):  # not from Tavletta, e.g. the proxy\n"
"            error = {\"code\": \"http_%d\" % response.status_code, \"message\": response.text}\n"
"        raise LabelError(response.status_code, error[\"code\"], error[\"message\"])\n"
"    return response\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"def print_assets(numbers, printer=\"it-cab\", rows=None):\n"
"    \"\"\"One label per asset number, in one job; returns the finished job.\"\"\"\n"
"    body = {\n"
"        \"label\": \"asset-tag\",\n"
"        \"printer\": printer,\n"
"        \"data_rows\": [{\"AssetNumber\": str(n)} for n in numbers],\n"
"        \"wait\": 30,\n"
"    }\n"
"    if rows:\n"
"        body[\"rows\"] = rows  # e.g. \"14-20\": only these rows\n"
"    for attempt in range(5):\n"
"        try:\n"
"            job = call(\"POST\", \"/print\", json=body).json()\n"
"            break\n"
"        except LabelError as e:\n"
"            # refused before it was queued: nothing printed, safe to retry\n"
"            if e.code not in (\"busy\", \"queue_full\") or attempt == 4:\n"
"                raise\n"
"            time.sleep(2**attempt)\n"
"    while job[\"state\"] not in FINAL:  # still printing after \"wait\"\n"
"        time.sleep(2)\n"
"        job = call(\"GET\", \"/jobs/\" + job[\"id\"]).json()\n"
"    return job\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"def preview(number, path=\"preview.png\"):\n"
"    body = {\"label\": \"asset-tag\", \"data_rows\": [{\"AssetNumber\": str(number)}]}\n"
"    with open(path, \"wb\") as file:\n"
"        file.write(call(\"POST\", \"/preview\", json=body).content)\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n"
"    preview(100001)\n"
"    numbers = range(100001, 100021)  # 20 labels\n"
"    job = print_assets(numbers)\n"
"    if job[\"state\"] == \"failed\":\n"
"        print(\"Stopped:\", job[\"error\"][\"message\"])\n"
"        # rows_printed rows are done: print the rest once the printer is fixed\n"
"        rest = \"%d-%d\" % (job[\"rows_printed\"] + 1, len(numbers))\n"
"        print(\"To continue:\", rest)\n"
"    else:\n"
"        print(job[\"state\"], job[\"printed\"], \"of\", job[\"total\"])\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/api-guide.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Example: C# and .NET { #csharp }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/api-guide.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "With `HttpClient` and `System.Net.Http.Json` (.NET 8 or newer), as a console program; in an application, register one `HttpClient` (for example with `IHttpClientFactory`) and reuse it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (csharp)
#: docs/api-guide.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"using System.Net;\n"
"using System.Net.Http.Headers;\n"
"using System.Net.Http.Json;\n"
"using System.Text;\n"
"using System.Text.Json;\n"
"using System.Text.Json.Serialization;\n"
"\n"
"var baseUrl = Environment.GetEnvironmentVariable(\"TAVLETTA\") ?? \"https://labels.example.com/api/v1\";\n"
"var token = Environment.GetEnvironmentVariable(\"TAVLETTA_TOKEN\")!; // from the secret store\n"
"\n"
"using var http = new HttpClient { BaseAddress = new Uri(baseUrl.TrimEnd('/') + \"/\"), Timeout = TimeSpan.FromSeconds(330) };\n"
"http.DefaultRequestHeaders.Authorization = new AuthenticationHeaderValue(\"Bearer\", token);\n"
"http.DefaultRequestHeaders.AcceptLanguage.ParseAdd(\"de-CH\");\n"
"var labels = new LabelClient(http);\n"
"\n"
"var numbers = Enumerable.Range(100001, 20).Select(n => n.ToString()).ToList();\n"
"var job = await labels.PrintAssetsAsync(numbers, \"it-cab\");\n"
"Console.WriteLine(job.State == \"failed\"\n"
"    ? $\"Stopped: {job.Error?.Message} To continue: rows {job.RowsPrinted + 1}-{numbers.Count}\"\n"
"    : $\"{job.State}: {job.Printed} of {job.Total}\");\n"
"\n"
"public record ApiError(string Code, string Message);\n"
"public record ErrorBody(ApiError Error);\n"
"public record Job(\n"
"    string Id, string State, int Printed, int Total,\n"
"    [property: JsonPropertyName(\"rows_printed\")] int RowsPrinted, ApiError? Error);\n"
"\n"
"public class LabelException(HttpStatusCode status, string code, string message) : Exception(message)\n"
"{\n"
"    public HttpStatusCode Status { get; } = status;\n"
"    public string Code { get; } = code;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"public class LabelClient(HttpClient http)\n"
"{\n"
"    static readonly JsonSerializerOptions Json = new(JsonSerializerDefaults.Web);\n"
"\n"
"    public async Task<Job> PrintAssetsAsync(IList<string> assetNumbers, string printer, string? rows = null)\n"
"    {\n"
"        var body = new Dictionary<string, object>\n"
"        {\n"
"            [\"label\"] = \"asset-tag\",\n"
"            [\"printer\"] = printer,\n"
"            [\"data_rows\"] = assetNumbers.Select(n => new Dictionary<string, string> { [\"AssetNumber\"] = n }),\n"
"            [\"wait\"] = 30,\n"
"        };\n"
"        if (rows != null) body[\"rows\"] = rows; // e.g. \"14-20\"\n"
"        Job job;\n"
"        for (var attempt = 0; ; attempt++)\n"
"        {\n"
"            try { job = await SendAsync<Job>(HttpMethod.Post, \"print\", body); break; }\n"
"            catch (LabelException e) when (e.Code is \"busy\" or \"queue_full\" && attempt < 4)\n"
"            {\n"
"                await Task.Delay(TimeSpan.FromSeconds(Math.Pow(2, attempt))); // nothing was printed\n"
"            }\n"
"        }\n"
"        while (job.State is \"queued\" or \"waiting\" or \"printing\")\n"
"        {\n"
"            await Task.Delay(2000);\n"
"            job = await SendAsync<Job>(HttpMethod.Get, $\"jobs/{job.Id}\");\n"
"        }\n"
"        return job;\n"
"    }\n"
"\n"
"    public Task<Job> CancelAsync(string jobId) => SendAsync<Job>(HttpMethod.Delete, $\"jobs/{jobId}\");\n"
"\n"
"    async Task<T> SendAsync<T>(HttpMethod method, string path, object? body = null)\n"
"    {\n"
"        using var request = new HttpRequestMessage(method, path);\n"
"        // as a string: the server needs a Content-Length (JsonContent would send it chunked)\n"
"        if (body != null)\n"
"            request.Content = new StringContent(JsonSerializer.Serialize(body), Encoding.UTF8, \"application/json\");\n"
"        using var response = await http.SendAsync(request);\n"
"        if (!response.IsSuccessStatusCode)\n"
"        {\n"
"            ErrorBody? error = null;\n"
"            try { error = await response.Content.ReadFromJsonAsync<ErrorBody>(Json); } catch (JsonException) { }\n"
"            throw new LabelException(response.StatusCode,\n"
"                error?.Error.Code ?? $\"http_{(int)response.StatusCode}\",\n"
"                error?.Error.Message ?? response.ReasonPhrase ?? \"\");\n"
"        }\n"
"        return (await response.Content.ReadFromJsonAsync<T>(Json))!;\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/api-guide.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "The base address ends with `/` and the paths have none at the start (`\"print\"`, `\"jobs/…\"`): `HttpClient` then keeps `/api/v1`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/api-guide.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "The body goes as a `StringContent`: the server needs a `Content-Length`, and `JsonContent.Create` would send the body in chunks without one (411 `length_required`)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: docs/api.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "API reference"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/api.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "The REST API of the print server (`tavletta serve`), for programs that print labels: every request with its role, fields, answers and error codes. A walkthrough for an inventory tool, with code in Python and C#, is [Connecting an inventory tool](api-guide.md); installing the server is [Server installation](server-install.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/api.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "This page is made from the OpenAPI 3.1 description of the server (`tools/openapi_docs.py`). Programs and code generators read the same description: `docs/openapi.yaml` in the source, or `GET /api/v1/openapi.json` from a running server."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/api.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Basics { #basics }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/api.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Address: `http://<server>:8790/api/v1`, or the HTTPS address of the reverse proxy. The examples use `$TAVLETTA` for it and `$TOKEN` for the access token:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: docs/api.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  TAVLETTA=https://labels.example.com/api/v1\n"
"  TOKEN=tav_0123456789ab_...\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/api.md
#, markdown-text
