#. type: Title #
#: docs/contribute.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Contribute"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/contribute.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Code, bug reports, translations and tests with other printers, cassettes and label rolls are welcome."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/contribute.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Issues and pull requests on [GitHub](https://github.com/joshii-h/tavletta) are welcome, no Forgejo account needed. They are copied automatically to [Forgejo](https://git.joshuahirsig.xyz/joshii/tavletta), the main repository, with a link on GitHub. Review and merge happen there; your commits are kept, so GitHub shows the pull request as merged. The discussion can stay on GitHub.  With a Forgejo account you can contribute there directly.  Details: [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://git.joshuahirsig.xyz/joshii/tavletta/src/branch/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/contribute.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "**App translations**: `tools/strings_<lang>.py`, see CONTRIBUTING."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/contribute.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "**This documentation**: `site/po/<lang>.po`, see [site/README.md](https://git.joshuahirsig.xyz/joshii/tavletta/src/branch/main/site/README.md).  Names of buttons and settings come from the app translation automatically."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/contribute.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Other printers**: printing goes through a backend interface; a new printer is a new backend. The protocols of the supported printers are described in [docs/](https://git.joshuahirsig.xyz/joshii/tavletta/src/branch/main/docs), one file per printer."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Tavletta"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Tavletta designs labels under Linux and prints them over the network or USB: on label printers with endless tape or die-cut labels, and on office printers, one label per page or on label sheets. It talks to each printer in its own language."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Tavletta is Romansh for a small tablet (from tavla, table/board). Pronounced tav-LET-ta."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Main window](media/main.png#only-light)  ![Main window](media/main-dark.png#only-dark)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Text, images, [symbols](use.md), QR codes and barcodes of many types; backgrounds printed edge to edge"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[Text styles](use.md#text-style), [lines and shapes](use.md#shapes), and a [free layout](use.md#free-layout) with each element at its own place; undo and redo"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Preview at print resolution: what you see is what is printed"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Endless tape as long as the content, or die-cut labels of any size"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[Serial labels](serial.md): one label for each row of a CSV, ODS or XLSX file; variables such as date and counter, and a command line"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[Label sheets](sheets.md) on office printers, and shipping labels from a carrier's PDF"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Finds the printer in the network and on USB, reads what is loaded and explains printer problems in plain words"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "A [print server](server.md) for other programs and AI assistants"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "27 languages, follows the light or dark mode of the desktop"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "The supported printers and what each one can do are listed under [Printers](printer.md). Further printers can be added as a backend, see [Contribute](contribute.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Install"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Flatpak"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Flathub is in preparation. Until then, build it yourself:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: docs/index.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"git clone https://git.joshuahirsig.xyz/joshii/tavletta.git && cd tavletta\n"
"flatpak install --user flathub org.gnome.Sdk//51 org.gnome.Platform//51\n"
"flatpak-builder --user --install --force-clean build-dir \\\n"
"    build-aux/flatpak/xyz.joshuahirsig.Tavletta.yml\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "install.sh"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Install the system packages, then run the script as your user (no root):"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Distribution | Packages |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| Debian, Ubuntu | `python3-gi gir1.2-gtk-4.0 gir1.2-adw-1 python3-gi-cairo python3-venv gettext` |\n"
"| Fedora | `python3-gobject gtk4 libadwaita python3-cairo gettext` |\n"
"| Arch | `python-gobject gtk4 libadwaita python-cairo gettext` |\n"
"| Gentoo | `dev-python/pygobject gui-libs/gtk:4 gui-libs/libadwaita dev-python/pycairo sys-devel/gettext` |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: docs/index.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"git clone https://git.joshuahirsig.xyz/joshii/tavletta.git && cd tavletta\n"
"./install.sh\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Uninstall: `./install.sh --uninstall` or `flatpak uninstall xyz.joshuahirsig.Tavletta`.  Saved labels and templates are kept."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "First label"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Switch the printer on and choose it under [[ui:Printer model]]. Tavletta finds it in the network (Bonjour) and reads what is loaded: the tape width or the distance between the labels."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Not found? Enter the address under [[ui:Host name or IP address]], e.g.  `printer.local` or `192.168.1.50`. New printer: connect it to the network first, see [Printers](printer.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Add]] text, an image or a code, then [[ui:Print]]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#: docs/index.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Save]] stores the label as `.tavletta` file, [[ui:Save as template…]] adds it to [[ui:Templates]]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Printers and troubleshooting"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Choose the printer under [[ui:Printer model]]; each one has its own section below."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "All printers { #common }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:No printer found]]: printer on and in the same network? The search needs the Avahi service (installed on most desktops, any init system); systemd-resolved alone resolves `.local` names but cannot search. Otherwise enter the address under [[ui:Host name or IP address]]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Printer not reachable]]: check the address, the printer may have a new IP. Switch the printer off and on again. On USB: check the cable and search again."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "No permission for the USB port: your user needs to be in the group `lp`.  Run `sudo usermod -aG lp $USER`, then log out and in again. NIIMBOT printers use another group, see [NIIMBOT](#niimbot)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "USB printer not found: check the cable, switch the printer on and wake it up (a sleeping printer can drop off USB), then search again."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "\"The printer is busy\" on USB: only one program can use a USB printer at a time. Close other label software, or wait until the running print is done."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Printer needs attention]]: the printer is reachable but reports a problem, the text below says what to do. Clear it on the printer, then [[ui:Refresh]]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Content cut off at the edge or askew: increase the [[ui:Safety margin]]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:content scaled down to fit]]: the content does not fit the label.  Make the label longer or larger, use [[ui:Automatic length]] on tape, or shorten the content."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Brother VC-500W { #vc500w }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Wi-Fi setup { #wifi }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Tavletta does not set up Wi-Fi. Use a phone or the printer's web interface once:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Hold the Wi-Fi button until it turns from blue to white."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Connect phone or computer to the open network \"Brother VC-500W…\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Open `https://192.168.0.1` (accept the certificate warning) or Brother's Color Label Editor app."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Choose your network and enter the password. Only 2.4 GHz, WPA or open."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Later, the web interface is at `https://` and the printer's address: \"Network Wi-Fi Setup\" changes the network (or \"click here\" to enter it by hand), \"AirPrint Options\" sets name, location and firmware updates."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "USB { #vc500w-usb }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Plug the printer in; [[ui:Search for printers]] finds it. Printing over USB has not been tried on a printer yet and follows the observations of others: the printer may not answer over USB at all (then the query ends with [[ui:Printer not reachable]]), and it may not cut by itself, then swipe across its panel. Wi-Fi is the tried way."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Cassettes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
