"| Cassette | Width |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| CZ-1001 | 9 mm (3/8″) |\n"
"| CZ-1002 | 12 mm (1/2″) |\n"
"| CZ-1003 | 19 mm (3/4″) |\n"
"| CZ-1004 | 25 mm (1″) |\n"
"| CZ-1005 | 50 mm (2″) |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Tavletta shows the inserted cassette, remaining tape, printable width, lot number and the presumed production date. ZINK paper ages: old paper prints paler and yellowish, Tavletta warns about old cassettes. Store cassettes cool and dry."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Cleaning: insert the cleaning cassette CK-1000, cleaning starts by itself.  Do it when stripes appear, or every 20 to 30 labels."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Print options { #vc500w-print }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Cut]]: [[ui:Full cut]] separates the labels. [[ui:Half cut]] cuts through the label, the backing holds them together. [[ui:No cut]]: the printer waits, swipe its panel to cut."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Colours]]: [[ui:Vivid]] for the strongest colours, [[ui:Normal]] (Brother: Standard) for softer ones, black and white (400 lpi) for text and codes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Colour correction: brightness and colour balance (red, green, blue), for this print only, not stored in the printer."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Problems { #vc500w-problems }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Wrong cassette]]: the label was designed for another width. Change [[ui:Tape width]] or the cassette."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:No cassette inserted]] or cassette not recognised: reinsert the cassette until it clicks."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "No paper: the cassette is empty, replace it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Paper jam: open the cover, remove the jammed label, reinsert the cassette."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Cover open: close the cover."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Warming up, cooling down, cleaning: wait, printing continues by itself."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Swipe the panel to cut: the label was printed without cut, swipe across the panel."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Pale colours, yellow tint: old paper (see the cassette's age), or [[ui:Normal]] instead of [[ui:Vivid]]. With old cassettes try [[ui:Brightness]] −1 to −3 under [[ui:Colour adjustment]]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Background barely visible: ZINK hardly prints very light pastel shades, choose a medium shade."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Stripes: clean with the CK-1000."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Content askew: insert the cassette straight."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Brother QL { #brother-ql }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Tavletta prints on Brother QL label printers from the QL-500 to the QL-1115NWB, red and black too on the QL-800, QL-810W and QL-820NWB. This has not been tried on a printer yet: it follows the protocol as others documented it. Reports of what works and what does not are very welcome."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Printer model]]: the QL appears twice. Choose \"Brother QL, continuous rolls\" for continuous DK rolls (the label is as long as its content or has a fixed length) and \"Brother QL, die-cut labels\" for die-cut DK labels of a fixed size.  Both use the same printer and settings. If the printer has the other kind of roll loaded, Tavletta offers to [[ui:Switch]]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Network: models with Wi-Fi or LAN are reached on port 9100.  [[ui:Search for printers]] finds them, or enter the address."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "USB: plug the printer in; [[ui:Search for printers]] finds it. On the QL-700 and the QL-800 series, switch off \"Editor Lite\" first (hold its button until the green light goes out), otherwise the printer appears as a USB drive."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Before each print Tavletta reads which roll is loaded. A continuous roll of another width is printed scaled to it after a warning ([[ui:Wrong roll]]); die-cut labels of another size get a warning too ([[ui:Different labels loaded]])."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Die-cut labels: choose the [[ui:Label size]] of the roll. The printer finds the labels by itself; leave the [[ui:Gap]] at 3 mm. About 1.5 mm at the sides and 3 mm at both ends of each label cannot be printed: a [[ui:Safety margin]] of 3 mm keeps content away from there."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Black and white without dithering: text and codes stay sharp, photos become hard black and white, as the preview shows."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Print options { #brother-ql-print }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Cut]]: [[ui:Full cut]] after every label, [[ui:Cut after the last label]] keeps the copies together as one strip, [[ui:No cut]]. The QL-500 has no cutter and no cut option."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Colours]]: [[ui:Red and black]] appears on the QL-800 series when a 62 mm continuous roll is loaded; red parts of the label print red on the red and black roll DK-22251. That roll needs a red and black job even for black labels: if the choice does not fit the loaded roll, the printer refuses the job, Tavletta prints it the other way and says so.  From then on the choice follows the roll."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Red and black: red parts stay red; images, the background and everything else are converted as for black-and-white printers, see [Black-and-white printers](use.md#black-and-white)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Quality]]: [[ui:High resolution (600 dpi)]] doubles the resolution along the roll; printing takes longer. Offered on the QL-570, QL-580N, QL-700, QL-710W, QL-720NW, the QL-800 series and the QL-1100 series."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Problems { #brother-ql-problems }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Reachable · the printer reports no status]]: some models do not answer status requests over the network. Printing works, but Tavletta cannot check the roll first."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "\"The loaded roll does not match the label\": a die-cut roll is loaded for a label on continuous roll, or the other way round. Load the other roll or choose the other entry under [[ui:Printer model]]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Out of labels: load a new roll. Cover open: close it. Label jammed: open the cover and remove it, check the cutter."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Red parts print black: red and black only works on the QL-800 series with the DK-22251 roll."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "cab label printers { #cab }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Tavletta prints on cab printers with a 4 inch print head: EOS2, EOS5, SQUIX 4 and MACH 4S, at 203, 300 or 600 dpi. Developed with an EOS2/300."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Network: the printer needs an address in your network (DHCP or set on its display). Tavletta uses the \"RawIP\" port 9100 with the JScript interpreter, both are the printer's defaults (Setup > Interfaces > Network services and Setup > Interpreter)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "USB: plug the printer in; [[ui:Search for printers]] finds it. Printing over USB has not been tried on a printer yet."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Labels: die-cut labels with a gap, label sensor \"Gap Sensor\". Tavletta sets the sensor for each job. Continuous media and a cutter are not supported yet."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Print method]]: [[ui:As set on the printer]] keeps the printer's own setting. [[ui:Thermal transfer (ribbon)]] for labels printed with a ribbon, [[ui:Thermal direct]] for labels that print without one. The printer then prints at the speed set on it, if its web interface tells it, else at 50 mm/s. [[ui:Printer details]] show the method set on the printer."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Print upside down]]: the label comes out turned by 180°, as the manufacturer's label software prints it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Heat and tear-off position stay as set on the printer."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Problems { #cab-problems }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Different labels loaded]]: the printer measured another distance between the labels than height plus gap of your label. Check [[ui:Label size]] and [[ui:Gap]], or load the right roll. Press Feed on the printer once after changing the roll so it measures again."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "A print that stopped because of a problem is cancelled, so printing again does not give extra labels."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Out of labels: load a new roll, the printer then synchronises by itself."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Print head open: close the print head."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Next label not found: labels not threaded through the label sensor, or labels without gaps (continuous media is not supported yet)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Ribbon problem: no ribbon in thermal transfer mode, or a ribbon in thermal direct mode. Load or remove the ribbon, or choose the other [[ui:Print method]]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Labels with a ribbon print blank or smeared, the ribbon does not move: the printer is set to thermal direct. Choose [[ui:Thermal transfer (ribbon)]] under [[ui:Print method]]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Paused: resume the printer on its display."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Print too pale or too dark: change the heat level in the printer's setup."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Brother P-touch { #ptouch }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Tavletta prints on Brother P-touch tape printers with TZe tape and HSe heat-shrink tube: the PT-P700, PT-P750W, PT-E550W, PT-P710BT, the PT-P900 series, the PT-D series and older models such as the PT-2430PC. Not tried on a printer yet."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "USB: plug the printer in; [[ui:Search for printers]] finds it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Network (PT-P750W, PT-E550W, PT-P900W, PT-P950NW): the search finds the printer, or enter its address. Tavletta uses port 9100."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Bluetooth is not supported; models with Bluetooth print over USB."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Editor Lite: with the Editor Lite lamp on, the printer is a USB drive and cannot print. Switch Editor Lite off, then search again."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Tape { #ptouch-tape }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Tavletta shows the inserted tape, its type (laminated, heat-shrink tube, ...) and the printable width under [[ui:Printer details]]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "The label fills the printable part of the tape. The edges of the tape stay blank: on 12 mm tape about 9.9 mm are printed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Heat-shrink tube: choose the nearest [[ui:Tape width]] (12 mm for an 11.2 mm tube)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Print in black: on coloured tape the tape's ink colour prints. Images are printed in black and white without dithering."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Print options { #ptouch-print }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Cut]]: [[ui:Full cut]] cuts each label off. [[ui:Half cut]] cuts through the label, the backing holds the labels together. [[ui:No cut]] prints the labels as one strip. The strip is cut after the last label.  Models with a cutter lever have no cut setting."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Chain printing]]: the last label stays in the printer and comes out with the next print. Saves about 25 mm of tape per print."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:High resolution]]: finer print along the tape, slower."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Tape feed]]: blank tape before and after each label, at least 2 mm (PT-P900 series: 1 mm)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "The first label after switching on starts with a blank piece: the cutter sits behind the print head."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Problems { #ptouch-problems }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Wrong cassette]]: another tape width is inserted. The label is scaled to the tape."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Cover open, no tape, tape not recognised: close the cover, insert the tape until it clicks."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Batteries low: connect the power adapter."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Print head too hot: wait a few minutes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Model not supported: Tavletta knows the models listed above."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "NIIMBOT { #niimbot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Tavletta prints on NIIMBOT label printers over USB: B1, B21, B3S, B4, D11, D110, D101 and related models. It has not been tried on a printer yet; please report how it works."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "USB: plug the printer in and switch it on; [[ui:Search for printers]] finds it. Otherwise enter its port, for example `/dev/ttyACM0`, under [[ui:Host name or IP address]]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "The port belongs to the group `dialout` (Fedora, Debian, Ubuntu) or `uucp` (Arch Linux), not `lp`. Run `sudo usermod -aG dialout $USER` (on Arch Linux: `uucp`), then log out and in again."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Bluetooth is not supported yet. Older B3S with a micro-USB port do not answer over USB; the B3S P with USB-C does."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Label size]]: the labels on the roll, the width across the printer.  On the D11, D110 and D101 the roll is narrow (12 mm on a D11): choose [[ui:Along the roll]] under [[ui:Content direction]] for text along the label."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "A label narrower than the print head is printed in its middle. One a little wider is cut to the middle: a B1 prints 48 mm of a 50 mm label.  Keep 1 mm or more as [[ui:Safety margin]]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "In the printer group: [[ui:Print density]] (higher prints darker) and [[ui:Label sensor]] (labels with gaps, black marks, a continuous roll or transparent labels, as loaded). Tavletta offers what the connected model takes and remembers the choice."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Problems { #niimbot-problems }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "No permission for the serial port: add your user to the group, see above."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Printer not reachable]] right after plugging in: some systems probe new serial ports for a modem first. Wait a few seconds, then [[ui:Refresh]]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Cover open, out of labels or a low battery: close the cover, load a roll or charge the printer, then [[ui:Refresh]]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Printing fails after some copies: the message says how many labels were already printed. The job is canceled, nothing prints later on its own."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "The printer is found, but printing reports an unknown model: Tavletta does not know its model number yet. Please [[ui:Report a problem…]], the report contains the number."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "System printer (CUPS, IPP) { #system }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Prints on the printers your computer knows: printers set up in the system settings (also over USB) and printers in the network that support IPP Everywhere or AirPrint, as most office printers do. The label is printed as one page of exactly its size, unscaled."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Search for printers]] lists both. Otherwise enter the printer's address or the name of its CUPS queue under [[ui:Host name or IP address]]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Label size]]: the paper size, or [[ui:Custom size]]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Print on]] [[ui:Label sheet]]: several labels on a sheet of self-adhesive labels, see [Label sheets](sheets.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Most office printers cannot print the outer 4 to 5 mm of a page: set the [[ui:Safety margin]] to 5 mm. On label sheets Tavletta warns when a label reaches into what the printer reports."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Problems { #system-problems }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Out of paper, paper jam or cover open while printing: Tavletta shows it and waits. Fix it at the printer within 5 minutes and printing goes on."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Out of toner or ink, or a problem before printing: fix it as the printer's display shows, then [[ui:Refresh]]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Printing fails after some copies: the message says how many labels were already printed. The rest is canceled, nothing prints later on its own."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "The label is printed smaller or moved: the printer or its driver scales the page. Turn off \"fit to page\" in the printer's setup."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Other jobs are printing first: Tavletta says the label was sent, and the printer prints it when its turn comes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "The job is held in the queue (until it is released, or until a password is entered): Tavletta cancels it. Check the queue in the system settings."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Label printers with ZPL, EPL2, TSPL, ESC/POS or DYMO { #raw }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Tavletta prints on label printers that take the label as an image in their own printer language. These printers have not been tried with Tavletta yet: if you have one, a report of what works and what does not helps a lot ([[ui:Report a problem…]])."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Printer model in Tavletta | Printers |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| Zebra ZPL | Zebra GK, GX, ZD, ZT and other printers with ZPL, also ZPL compatible printers of other makers |\n"
"| Zebra EPL2 | Zebra LP/TLP 2824 and 2844, GK420 and GX420 set to EPL2 |\n"
"| TSPL (TSC, Munbyn, iDPRT, Xprinter, Rollo) | TSC printers and most 4 × 6 in shipping label printers |\n"
"| [[ui:Receipt printer (ESC/POS)]] | Epson TM and compatible receipt printers on 58 or 80 mm paper |\n"
"| DYMO LabelWriter | LabelWriter 300, 400 and 450 series, 4XL (not the 550 and 5XL) |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Connection: over the network on port 9100, or USB. Plug a USB printer in and use [[ui:Search for printers]]. Some low-cost shipping label printers do not show up as a printer on USB; Tavletta cannot find those."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Resolution]]: choose the resolution of the print head (203, 300 or 600 dpi). Zebra printers report it: [[ui:As reported by the printer]]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Label sensor]]: [[ui:As set on the printer]] keeps the printer's own setting. [[ui:Gap between labels]] for die-cut labels, [[ui:Black mark]] for labels with a black mark on the back, [[ui:Continuous media]] for a roll without gaps. Set the [[ui:Label size]] and the [[ui:Gap]] (or the height of the mark) like the roll."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:After printing]]: [[ui:Tear off]], [[ui:Peel off]] or [[ui:Cut off]], if the printer has a peeler or a cutter.  [[ui:As set on the printer]] leaves the printer's own setting."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Darkness]] and [[ui:Speed]] change the printer's setting for this print; [[ui:As set on the printer]] leaves it alone."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Print upside down]]: for a printer that puts out the label the wrong way round."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Receipt printers print the label on endless paper: choose the paper width under [[ui:Tape width]]. The printable width is narrower than the paper (48 mm on 58 mm paper, 72 mm on 80 mm paper). [[ui:Cut]] in the print dialog cuts the paper after each label."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Problems { #raw-problems }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Reachable · the printer reports no status]]: the printer takes jobs but answers no questions, which many of these printers do (EPL2 printers never answer). Problems such as an open cover then show on the printer only."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "The printer did not report its resolution in time: choose it under [[ui:Resolution]] instead of [[ui:As reported by the printer]]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "The label comes out upside down: switch on [[ui:Print upside down]], and please report it with the printer model; the orientation could not be tried on a printer yet."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Print too pale or too dark: change [[ui:Darkness]]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "The printer prints several blank labels or stops between labels: the [[ui:Label sensor]] does not match the roll, or the printer has to measure the labels again (most printers do that with a long press on Feed)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Nothing is printed and the printer shows no problem: check that its printer language is the one chosen in Tavletta (many printers can switch between ZPL and EPL2, or between TSPL and ESC/POS)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Help"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/printer.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Something else? [[ui:Report a problem…]] in the main menu (also offered with error messages) opens a prefilled issue in the browser with version, system and printer. You see everything before sending it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: docs/serial.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Serial labels"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/serial.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "One label for each row of a table: inventory numbers, shelf labels, name badges, addresses. The label holds placeholders such as `{Name}`; each printed label shows the values of its row."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/serial.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Serial labels](media/serial.png#only-light)  ![Serial labels](media/serial-dark.png#only-dark)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/serial.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Data file"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/serial.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Data for serial labels…]] in the main menu, [[ui:Choose…]] under [[ui:Serial labels]], or drop the file onto the window."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/serial.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "CSV (comma, semicolon or tab), ODS (LibreOffice) or XLSX (Excel). The first filled row holds the column names."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/serial.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "A title above the column names counts as the first row: delete it, or put the table on a sheet of its own."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/serial.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "ODS: cells as LibreOffice shows them, dates as `2026-11-11`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/serial.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "XLSX: numbers with their decimals, leading zeros and percent signs, dates as `2026-11-11`. Thousands separators and text in the number format, such as a currency, are left out. Dates in the East Asian built-in formats come out as numbers."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/serial.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Empty rows are left out. The hidden cells of merged cells are empty."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/serial.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Several sheets: choose one under [[ui:Sheet]]. If the sheet saved with the label is no longer there, nothing is printed until another one is chosen."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/serial.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Read again]] after the file was changed in the spreadsheet program."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/serial.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Up to 100 000 rows, 1000 columns, 2 000 000 cells (rows times columns, without the row of column names) and 50 MB."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/serial.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "The label file stores where the data file is, never its content. If the data file lies in the same folder as the label (or below it), both can be moved or shared together. If it is missing when the label is opened, Tavletta says so: choose it again or remove it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/serial.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "A data file is read without asking only if it is a table (`.csv`, `.tsv`, `.txt`, `.ods`, `.xlsx`) in the label's folder or below, and not in a hidden folder. Any other data file is read only after asking, once for each label file: a label from someone else could name any file.  [[ui:Forget allowed data files]] in the main menu makes Tavletta ask again."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/serial.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "In the Flatpak, Tavletta sees only the files it is given: a label opened from the file manager or the file chooser, but not the folder around it.  A data file beside the label is then not found: choose it with [[ui:Data for serial labels…]] (the file chooser gives Tavletta access to it)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/serial.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Templates keep the placeholders but not the data file. Older versions of Tavletta refuse labels with a data file instead of printing the placeholders."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/serial.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Placeholders"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/serial.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Insert column]] next to a text or the content of a code adds `{Column}` at the cursor; typing it works as well."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/serial.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Placeholders work in texts and in QR codes and barcodes, for example `https://example.org/item/{Number}`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/serial.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "With a data file `{{` and `}}` print a single brace, in every text and code: `{{Name}}` prints `{Name}`. Other braces need doubling too, for example JSON in a QR code: `{{\"id\":{Number}}}`. Without a data file texts print as typed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/serial.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Values are printed as they are, even if they contain braces."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/serial.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "A placeholder without a column of that name is printed as it is; the line under the preview names it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/serial.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Before printing, the codes of every row are checked: an EAN-13 needs 12 or 13 digits, an empty cell gives no code. Rows that fail are named; print without them or correct the data file."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/serial.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Variables such as `{=counter}` or `{=date}` work together with the placeholders; the counter goes on from row to row."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/serial.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Preview"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/serial.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "The buttons under the preview step through the rows: [[ui:First row]], [[ui:Previous row]], [[ui:Next row]] and [[ui:Last row]], or Alt+Page Up, Alt+Page Down, Alt+Home and Alt+End."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/serial.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Rows are counted without the row of column names."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/serial.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Export PNG…]] saves the row that is shown."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/serial.md docs/use.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Print"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/serial.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Print]] prints one label for each row. [[ui:From row]] and [[ui:To row]] limit the rows (all of them by default), [[ui:Copies of each label]] sets how many of each are printed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/serial.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Every label is a print job of its own, so this works on every printer."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/serial.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[ui:Stop]] in the bar above the window ends the series after the label being printed; the first label is always printed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/serial.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "If the printer reports a problem, printing stops at that row; the message says how many copies of it were already printed. Solve the problem, then print again starting from that row."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/serial.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "On a label sheet each position gets one label: the rows in order, the copies of a row on the positions after each other, starting at the positions chosen for the first sheet. All sheets are one print job, so [[ui:Stop]] is not offered. After a problem the message also says at which position of which sheet the row to go on from belongs."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/serial.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Command line"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/serial.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "`tavletta print shelf.tavletta --data items.csv --rows 3-10` prints rows 3 to 10 without opening a window; see [Command line](use.md#command-line).  With `--dry-run` each line of the listing starts with the row number."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Server installation"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "This guide sets up the print server (`tavletta serve`) on a Linux server for a company: other programs, for example an inventory tool, print labels through it over the network. What the server does and how programs use it: [Print server](server.md) and [API reference](api.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Overview { #overview }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "One small service: a REST API (and MCP for AI assistants) on port 8790.  It renders the labels itself and sends them to the printers over the network; no desktop, no browser, no database."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "The printers it may use are named in `printers.toml`; no other address can be printed on."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Every program or device gets its own access token with a role (`tokens.toml`); the file keeps only a fingerprint (hash) of each token."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "The labels are `.tavletta` files in a labels folder, designed in the Tavletta app and copied there."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "It listens on `127.0.0.1` only. Other computers reach it through a reverse proxy with HTTPS (Traefik, nginx, Caddy)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Requirements { #requirements }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "A Linux server on x86-64 or ARM64 (a virtual machine or a Raspberry Pi 4/5 is enough)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Either Docker Engine with the Compose plugin (option A, recommended), or Python 3.11 or newer with PyGObject, Pango and Cairo from the distribution (option B)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Resources: 1 CPU core, 1 GB RAM reserved (the server usually uses 50–150 MB; a large label is limited to 40 megapixels), 500 MB of disk for the image or the installation, plus the labels."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Network from the server to the printers:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  | Printer | Port |\n"
"  |---|---|\n"
"  | cab, Brother QL, ZPL, EPL2, TSPL, ESC/POS, DYMO and others printing \"raw\" | TCP 9100 |\n"
"  | Office printers and CUPS queues (IPP) | TCP 631 |\n"
"  | Brother VC-500W | TCP 9100 |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Only for finding printers automatically (mDNS) or USB printers: the host's network (option A with `compose.host.yaml`) or a native installation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Fonts: every font the labels use must be installed on the server (see [Fonts](#fonts))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Option A: Docker Compose { #docker }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "1. Get the files and the image { #docker-build }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: docs/server-install.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"sudo git clone https://git.joshuahirsig.xyz/joshii/tavletta.git /opt/tavletta\n"
"cd /opt/tavletta\n"
"sudo git checkout v1.1.0      # the release to run: git tag lists them\n"
"cd packaging/docker\n"
"sudo docker compose pull      # ghcr.io/joshii-h/tavletta:1.1, for x86-64 and ARM64\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "The image (about 230 MB), built and tested by the project's CI and signed (see [Server and container](server.md#container)), contains Tavletta, Python, Pango and Cairo, the fonts DejaVu, Source Sans 3, Liberation (metrics of Arial, Times New Roman and Courier New) and Carlito (metrics of Calibri). It runs as an unprivileged user, read-only, without capabilities."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "2. Folders { #docker-folders }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Everything that belongs to your installation lives in three folders next to `compose.yaml` (git ignores them):"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (text)
#: docs/server-install.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"/opt/tavletta/packaging/docker/\n"
"├── compose.yaml\n"
"├── config/          printers.toml, tokens.toml\n"
"├── labels/          the label files (.tavletta) and their data files\n"
"└── fonts/           fonts of your own (.ttf, .otf), may stay empty\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: docs/server-install.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"sudo mkdir -p config labels fonts\n"
"sudo chown -R 1000:1000 config labels fonts\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "The container runs as user 1000 (set `TAVLETTA_UID` and `TAVLETTA_GID` for another one): it reads `config/` and saves counters into the label files of `labels/`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "3. Printers: printers.toml { #printers }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "`config/printers.toml` names every printer programs may use. An example with a cab printer for asset labels (thermal transfer, printed turned by 180 degrees), a Brother QL at the reception and an office printer over IPP:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (toml)
#: docs/server-install.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[printers.it-cab]\n"
"backend = \"cab\"                          # cab EOS, SQUIX, MACH\n"
"host = \"cab-it.example.com\"              # name or IP address of the printer\n"
"description = \"Asset labels\"\n"
"location = \"IT store room\"\n"
"media = \"57 x 32 mm polyester, resin ribbon\"\n"
"default = true                           # used when a request names no printer\n"
"max_copies = 50\n"
"\n"
"[printers.it-cab.settings]\n"
"method = \"transfer\"                      # thermal transfer with ribbon (direct: without)\n"
"upside_down = true                       # printed turned by 180 degrees\n"
"\n"
"[printers.reception-ql]\n"
"backend = \"brother_ql\"                   # Brother QL-700, QL-8xx, QL-1100 …\n"
"host = \"192.0.2.21\"\n"
"description = \"Visitor and sample labels\"\n"
"location = \"Reception\"\n"
"media = \"DK-22205, 62 mm continuous\"\n"
"max_copies = 20\n"
"cut = \"full\"\n"
"\n"
"[printers.reception-ql.settings]\n"
"quality = \"high\"\n"
"\n"
"[printers.office]\n"
"backend = \"system\"                       # any IPP printer or CUPS queue\n"
"host = \"ipp://office-printer.example.com/ipp/print\"\n"
"description = \"Label sheets, A4\"\n"
"max_copies = 10\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "`backend` is the printer model: `cab`, `brother_ql`, `brother_ql_diecut`, `ptouch`, `vc500w`, `zpl`, `epl`, `tspl`, `escpos`, `dymo`, `niimbot`, `system` (`tavletta list-printers` shows them)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "`host` is the printer's name or IP address; for `system` an IPP address. Give printers a fixed address (DHCP reservation or DNS name)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "The settings of a model are those of the app's printer settings; the full list is in [docs/server.md](https://git.joshuahirsig.xyz/joshii/tavletta/src/branch/main/docs/server.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "A mistake stops the server with the file, the key and the problem, for example `printers.toml: printers.it-cab.settings.method: expected one of: printer, transfer, direct`. Changes need a restart."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "4. Access tokens: tokens.toml { #tokens }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Create one token per program or device. The token is shown once; the file keeps only its hash."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: docs/server-install.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"sudo docker run --rm --user 1000:1000 -v ./config:/config --entrypoint tavletta \\\n"
"    ghcr.io/joshii-h/tavletta:1.1 token new inventory-tool --role print --printer it-cab \\\n"
"    --description \"Inventory tool\" \\\n"
"    --tokens /config/tokens.toml --printers /config/printers.toml\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (text)
#: docs/server-install.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"tav_3f9c0a1b2c4d_Xq2…\n"
"tavletta: The token is shown only this once; /config/tokens.toml keeps only its hash.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Give the token to the program's administrator over a safe channel (a password manager), never by e-mail."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Roles: `preview` (look only), `print` (also print, see its own jobs), `admin` (see and cancel every job). Give programs `print`, monitoring `preview`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "`--printer` (repeatable) limits the token to these printers; `--expires 2027-12-31` to a date."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Always pass `--printers`: once a token is limited to printers, the file can only be checked with the printer list."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "New tokens work at once, without a restart. To revoke one, delete its entry from `config/tokens.toml`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "5. Labels { #labels }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Design the labels in the Tavletta app and copy the `.tavletta` files into `labels/` (subfolders are allowed). Programs name them without the ending: `labels/inventory/asset-tag.tavletta` is `\"label\": \"inventory/asset-tag\"`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: docs/server-install.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"sudo cp asset-tag.tavletta labels/\n"
"sudo chown 1000:1000 labels/asset-tag.tavletta\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "6. Start { #docker-start }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: docs/server-install.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"sudo docker compose up -d\n"
"sudo docker compose ps\n"
"curl http://127.0.0.1:8790/api/v1/health\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (text)
#: docs/server-install.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "{\"status\": \"ok\", \"version\": \"1.1.0\"}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "The container restarts by itself after a crash or a reboot."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Set the time zone of `{=date}` and `{=time}` on labels with `TAVLETTA_TZ=Europe/Zurich` in a file `.env` next to `compose.yaml` (UTC by default)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Check the token and the printers:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: docs/server-install.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  TOKEN=tav_3f9c0a1b2c4d_Xq2…\n"
"  curl -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" http://127.0.0.1:8790/api/v1/printers\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Each printer is listed with its state; `UNREACHABLE` with a message if\n"
"  the server cannot reach it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Host network: mDNS and USB { #docker-host }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "To find printers on the network by mDNS, to print on CUPS queues of the host or on USB printers, start with the override `compose.host.yaml`:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: docs/server-install.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "sudo docker compose -f compose.yaml -f compose.host.yaml up -d\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The container then shares the host's network and listens on\n"
"`127.0.0.1:8790` of the host. CUPS queues of the host are\n"
"`ipp://localhost:631/printers/<queue>` in `printers.toml`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Logs { #docker-logs }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: docs/server-install.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "sudo docker compose logs -f\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Each request is logged with the client's address, the token's name, the path and the status; each job with its label, printer and outcome. Tokens and label contents are never logged."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Updating { #docker-update }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: docs/server-install.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"cd /opt/tavletta\n"
"sudo git fetch --tags\n"
"sudo git checkout v1.2.0         # the new release\n"
"cd packaging/docker\n"
"sudo docker compose pull\n"
"sudo docker compose up -d\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Read the release notes first. Waiting jobs are canceled when the server stops; a label being printed is finished. `config/`, `labels/` and `fonts/` are kept."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Backup { #docker-backup }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Back up the three folders: `config/` (the printer list, the token hashes), `labels/` (the labels and their counters: the next number of each label with `{=counter}` is saved in its file) and `fonts/`. The image can be pulled again at any time."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Uninstalling { #docker-uninstall }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: docs/server-install.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"cd /opt/tavletta/packaging/docker\n"
"sudo docker compose down\n"
"sudo docker image rm ghcr.io/joshii-h/tavletta:1.1\n"
"sudo rm -r /opt/tavletta     # also deletes config, labels and fonts\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Option B: native with systemd { #native }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "For a server without Docker. Tested on Debian 13, Ubuntu 24.04 and Fedora 44. The installation needs internet access (Python packages from PyPI, one from GitHub)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "1. System packages { #native-packages }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Debian, Ubuntu:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: docs/server-install.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"sudo apt install python3 python3-venv python3-gi python3-gi-cairo gir1.2-pango-1.0 \\\n"
"    gettext git fontconfig fonts-dejavu-core\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Fedora:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: docs/server-install.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "sudo dnf install python3 python3-gobject gobject-introspection pango gettext git-core\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "No GTK is needed. `gettext` and `git` are needed only while installing."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "2. Install Tavletta { #native-install }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Into its own Python environment in `/opt/tavletta`, which uses the system's PyGObject:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: docs/server-install.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"sudo python3 -m venv --system-site-packages /opt/tavletta\n"
"sudo /opt/tavletta/bin/pip install \"git+https://git.joshuahirsig.xyz/joshii/tavletta.git@v1.1.0\"\n"
"/opt/tavletta/bin/tavletta --version\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "3. Service user and folders { #native-user }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: docs/server-install.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"sudo useradd --system --home-dir /var/lib/tavletta --create-home \\\n"
"    --shell /usr/sbin/nologin tavletta\n"
"sudo install -d -o tavletta -g tavletta -m 0750 /etc/tavletta /var/lib/tavletta/labels\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Path | Content | Owner, mode |\n"
"|---|---|---|\n"
"| `/etc/tavletta/printers.toml` | the printers ([as above](#printers)) | `tavletta`, 600 |\n"
"| `/etc/tavletta/tokens.toml` | the token hashes | `tavletta`, 600 |\n"
"| `/var/lib/tavletta/labels/` | the label files | `tavletta`, 750 |\n"
"| `/usr/local/share/fonts/` | fonts of your own | `root`, readable by all |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Create the tokens as the service user, so the file belongs to it:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: docs/server-install.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"sudo -u tavletta /opt/tavletta/bin/tavletta token new inventory-tool --role print \\\n"
"    --printer it-cab --tokens /etc/tavletta/tokens.toml --printers /etc/tavletta/printers.toml\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "The server refuses a `tokens.toml` that every user may change, and warns about one that others may read."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "4. The service { #native-service }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "`packaging/systemd/tavletta-server.service` runs the server as `tavletta`, sandboxed (read-only system, no home folders, no capabilities, 1 GB memory):"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: docs/server-install.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"sudo curl -fsSLo /etc/systemd/system/tavletta-server.service \\\n"
"    https://git.joshuahirsig.xyz/joshii/tavletta/raw/tag/v1.1.0/packaging/systemd/tavletta-server.service\n"
"sudo systemctl daemon-reload\n"
"sudo systemctl enable --now tavletta-server\n"
"systemctl status tavletta-server\n"
"curl http://127.0.0.1:8790/api/v1/health\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "`sudo systemctl reload tavletta-server` reads `tokens.toml` again (SIGHUP); it is also read again whenever it changes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "`sudo systemctl restart tavletta-server` after changing `printers.toml` or installing fonts."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Logs: `journalctl -u tavletta-server -f`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text
