#. type: Title ##
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Reverse proxy and HTTPS { #proxy }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "The server speaks plain HTTP on `127.0.0.1`. Other computers reach it through a reverse proxy that adds HTTPS. Give the server the proxy's address with `--trusted-proxy`, so the log and the limits per client see the real client, not the proxy."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Traefik (Docker) { #traefik }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Traefik and Tavletta in one Docker network, Traefik with a fixed address. In `compose.yaml`, remove `ports:` (the server is then reached only through Traefik) and add:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (yaml)
#: docs/server-install.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"services:\n"
"  tavletta:\n"
"    # ... as in compose.yaml, without ports:\n"
"    networks: [proxy]\n"
"    command:\n"
"      - \"--mcp\"\n"
"      - \"--printers\"\n"
"      - \"/config/printers.toml\"\n"
"      - \"--tokens\"\n"
"      - \"/config/tokens.toml\"\n"
"      - \"--trusted-proxy\"\n"
"      - \"172.30.0.10/32\"          # Traefik's address in the network\n"
"    labels:\n"
"      - \"traefik.enable=true\"\n"
"      - \"traefik.http.routers.tavletta.rule=Host(`labels.example.com`)\"\n"
"      - \"traefik.http.routers.tavletta.entrypoints=websecure\"\n"
"      - \"traefik.http.routers.tavletta.tls.certresolver=letsencrypt\"\n"
"      - \"traefik.http.services.tavletta.loadbalancer.server.port=8790\"\n"
"\n"
"networks:\n"
"  proxy:\n"
"    external: true                # Traefik's network, Traefik at 172.30.0.10\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "nginx { #nginx }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "The server on `127.0.0.1` answers only requests for a local host name (against DNS rebinding): nginx must not pass on the public name. Its default (`127.0.0.1:8790`) is right; do not add `proxy_set_header Host $host`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (nginx)
#: docs/server-install.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"server {\n"
"    listen 443 ssl;\n"
"    server_name labels.example.com;\n"
"    ssl_certificate     /etc/ssl/certs/labels.example.com.pem;\n"
"    ssl_certificate_key /etc/ssl/private/labels.example.com.key;\n"
"\n"
"    client_max_body_size 4m;           # as the server's --max-body\n"
"    location / {\n"
"        proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:8790;\n"
"        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;\n"
"        proxy_read_timeout 330s;       # print requests may wait up to 300 s\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Start the server with `--trusted-proxy 127.0.0.1/32` (append it to `ExecStart` in the service, or to `command:` in `compose.yaml`)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Caddy { #caddy }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Caddy passes on the public host name by default; set it to the server's own:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (text)
#: docs/server-install.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"labels.example.com {\n"
"    reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8790 {\n"
"        header_up Host {upstream_hostport}\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Caddy gets a certificate by itself. Start the server with `--trusted-proxy 127.0.0.1/32`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Firewall { #firewall }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Open only the proxy's port 443, and only for the networks that need it (the inventory tool's server, the clients' VLAN)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Port 8790 stays closed: the server listens on `127.0.0.1` (Docker publishes it on `127.0.0.1` only)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Outgoing from the server to the printers: TCP 9100 and 631."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Never make the server reachable from the internet."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Fonts { #fonts }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "A label is drawn with the fonts of the computer that prints it. A text in a font the server does not have is drawn in another one; the preview and the print job then warn with `font_missing` (for example `Element 2: the font Source Sans 3 is not installed – another font is used`)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Docker: the image has DejaVu, Source Sans 3, Liberation and Carlito.  Copy other fonts (`.ttf`, `.otf`, e.g. the corporate font) into `fonts/` and restart: `sudo docker compose restart`. More Debian font packages: build the image yourself, `sudo docker compose -f compose.yaml -f compose.build.yaml build --build-arg FONTS=\"fonts-dejavu-core fonts-adobe-sourcesans3 fonts-liberation fonts-crosextra-carlito fonts-noto-core\"`, then `up -d` with the same two files."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Native: install the distribution's font packages (Debian, Ubuntu: `fonts-adobe-sourcesans3`; Fedora: `adobe-source-sans-pro-fonts`) or copy the font files to `/usr/local/share/fonts/`, then `sudo fc-cache -f` and restart the service."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Check what the server has: `fc-list : family` (in the container: `sudo docker compose exec tavletta fc-list : family`)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server-install.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Fonts may need a license for use on a server; Source Sans 3, Liberation, Carlito, DejaVu and Noto are free."
msgstr ""

