#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Every request and error code: [API reference](api.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "A walkthrough for programs, with code in Python and C#: [Connecting an inventory tool](api-guide.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/server.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Start { #start }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: docs/server.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "tavletta serve --labels-dir ~/Labels\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "The server listens on `http://127.0.0.1:8790`, only on this computer."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Only label files in the labels folder (and its subfolders) can be used, with their data files. Without `--labels-dir`: `~/.local/share/tavletta/labels`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Printer address, safety margin and print settings are those set in the app."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "`--mcp` adds the connection for AI assistants at `/mcp`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Stop with Ctrl+C: waiting jobs are canceled, a label being printed is finished and the counter saved."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/server.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Printers { #printers }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Name the printers in a file `printers.toml` and start the server with `--printers printers.toml`. Programs then choose a printer by its name; no other printer can be used."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (toml)
#: docs/server.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  [printers.shipping]\n"
"  backend = \"cab\"\n"
"  host = \"cab-shipping.example.com\"\n"
"  description = \"Shipping labels\"\n"
"  location = \"Warehouse, gate 2\"\n"
"  default = true\n"
"  max_copies = 200\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "`backend` is the printer model, `host` the printer's address."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "The printer's settings, as in the app's printer settings, go into a table of their own; only the ones the model has:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (toml)
#: docs/server.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  [printers.inventory]\n"
"  backend = \"cab\"\n"
"  host = \"cab-it.example.com\"\n"
"\n"
"  [printers.inventory.settings]\n"
"  method = \"transfer\"\n"
"  upside_down = true\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "`method` is the [[ui:Print method]] (`printer`, `transfer`, `direct`), `upside_down` [[ui:Print upside down]]; others are `quality`, `chain`, `high_res`, `feed_mm`, `darkness`, `media` and `outlines`, see [docs/server.md](https://git.joshuahirsig.xyz/joshii/tavletta/src/branch/main/docs/server.md#printers)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Mistakes in the file are named when the server starts."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "The list of printers shows each printer with its state."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "The server searches the network for printers only when started with `--discover`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/server.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Access token { #token }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Create a token and keep it secret:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: docs/server.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  mkdir -p ~/.config/tavletta\n"
"  openssl rand -hex 32 > ~/.config/tavletta/token\n"
"  chmod 600 ~/.config/tavletta/token\n"
"  tavletta serve --token-file ~/.config/tavletta/token\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Every request then needs the header `Authorization: Bearer <token>`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "To listen on another address (`--host 0.0.0.0`), a token is required.  For other computers, put a reverse proxy with HTTPS in front."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "`--allow-printer` limits the printer addresses, for example `--allow-printer '*.local'`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/server.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Access per device { #tokens }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Several devices or people get a token each, with a role:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: docs/server.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  tavletta token new shipping-pc --role print --tokens ~/.config/tavletta/tokens.toml\n"
"  tavletta serve --printers printers.toml --tokens ~/.config/tavletta/tokens.toml\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "The token is shown only once; the file keeps only a fingerprint (hash)  of it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "`preview` only lists and shows previews, `print` also prints and follows its own jobs, `admin` sees and cancels all jobs."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "`--printer shipping` limits a token to that printer, `--expires 2027-12-31` to a date."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "To take a token back, delete its entry in `tokens.toml`. The server notices it at once."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/server.md
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Programs (REST API) { #api }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "The description of all requests: the [API reference](api.md), and for programs `http://127.0.0.1:8790/api/v1/openapi.json` (OpenAPI 3.1, with any valid token)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "`GET /api/v1/labels` lists the labels, `GET /api/v1/labels/<name>` shows what can be filled in: element names, variables and columns."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "`POST /api/v1/preview` returns the label as a PNG image."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "`POST /api/v1/print` queues a print job; `GET /api/v1/jobs/<id>` shows its state, `DELETE` cancels it between two labels."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Each printer prints one job after the other."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Messages come in the language of the `Accept-Language` header."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Without an access token, requests that ask printers need the header `X-Tavletta-Request: 1`, so that no web page can send them."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: docs/server.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"curl -H \"Authorization: Bearer $(cat ~/.config/tavletta/token)\" \\\n"
"     -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n"
"     -d '{\"label\": \"serial\", \"data_rows\": [{\"Code\": \"B-07-1\", \"Name\": \"Tea\", \"Shelf\": \"B-07\", \"Box\": \"1\"}], \"copies\": 2}' \\\n"
"     http://127.0.0.1:8790/api/v1/print\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "`set` fills in elements by their name and variables such as `{=lot}`, as on the command line."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "Serial labels: `\"data_rows\"`, one object per label with every column the label uses (`[{\"Name\": \"Tea\", …}, {\"Name\": \"Rice\", …}]`), or `\"data_file\"` with a table in the labels folder."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "One label from another program, for example an inventory: the fields as one data row, the printer by its name."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: docs/server.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  curl -H \"Authorization: Bearer $(cat ~/.config/tavletta/token)\" \\\n"
"       -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n"
"       -d '{\"label\": \"asset-tag\", \"printer\": \"it-cab\", \"copies\": 1,\n"
"            \"data_rows\": [{\"AssetNumber\": \"100001\"}]}' \\\n"
"       http://127.0.0.1:8790/api/v1/print\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "The whole walkthrough, with series, retries and code in Python and C#: [Connecting an inventory tool](api-guide.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/server.md
#, markdown-text
msgid "`{=counter}`: the server saves the next number in the label file. A program that keeps its own numbers sends the number in the data row or as `\"counter_start\"` with `\"no_save_counter\": true`."
msgstr ""

